through `uv run --with ...` because they aren't installed in `.venv`. The black run matched the version the project uses, and HEAD was already black-clean.\n\nWhat changed, all in `sqlite_utils/db.py`:\n\n- **`ForeignKey`** is a `@dataclass(order=True)` with `columns`, `other_columns`, `is_compound`, `on_delete` and `on_update`. It is no longer a tuple, so unpacking it or indexing it raises `TypeError`.\n- **Reading keys:** `Table.foreign_keys` groups `PRAGMA foreign_key_list` rows by `id`, orders them by `seq`, and reads the actions. A `REFERENCES other` with no columns resolves to the other table's primary key.\n- **Creating tables:** single keys stay inline, and compound keys become table-level `FOREIGN KEY (...) REFERENCES ...` lines. Actions are emitted as `ON UPDATE ... ON DELETE ...`.\n- **Adding keys:** `Database.add_foreign_keys` accepts `ForeignKey` objects and 4-tuples, and keeps actions. `Table.add_foreign_key` gained `on_delete`/`on_update` and accepts tuples of columns.\n- **Transform:** `drop_foreign_keys` takes a column name or an exact tuple. Renames and drops work per key, and actions and compound shape are preserved.\n- **Indexes:** `index_foreign_keys` creates one composite index per compound key.\n\nTwo calls the spec left open:\n- For a single key whose `REFERENCES` target has a different number of primary-key columns than the key has columns, I kept the unresolved `None` rather than guessing.\n- `add_foreign_keys` raises `ValueError` when a 4-tuple has mismatched column counts. The spec didn't name a message for this, so I reused the one `add_foreign_key` uses.", "ttft_ms": 1432, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 191727, "uuid": "aeac4c41-0994-4e07-9682-1f0e59c6aaf0", "ttft_stream_ms": 1204, "time_to_request_ms": 396, "first_content_frame_ms": 1204, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
